        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: What sport is Pekka Niemi known for?\n\nAnswer A: cross-country skier\n  about: Pekka Niemi (skier)\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Pekka Niemi (skier) Juho Pekka Niemi (born \"Yliniemi\", 15 November 1909 – 21 December 1993) was a Finnish cross-country skier who competed at the 1936 Winter Olympics.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: cross-country skiing\n  about: Pekka Niemi (skier)\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"1939 World Championships , where he placed fifth over 50 km and sixth over 18 km . He was a forest manager by profession .\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Pekka Niemi (skier) Juho Pekka Niemi (born \"Yliniemi\", 15 November 1909 – 21 December 1993) was a Finnish cross-country skier who competed at the 1936 Winter Olympics. He won a bronze medal in the 18 km event and placed eighth over 50 km. His biggest success came at the 1937 FIS Nordic World Ski Championships, where he won a complete set of medals: a gold in the 50 km, a silver in the 4×10 km relay and a bronze in the 18 km. He also won the 50 km race at the 1938 Holmenkollen ski festival. Niemi won only one\nDocument 2: 1939 World Championships , where he placed fifth over 50 km and sixth over 18 km . He was a forest manager by profession . [ 1 ] Cross-country skiing results [ edit ] All results are sourced from the International Ski Federation ( FIS ) . [ 2 ] Olympic Games [ edit ] 1 medal – ( 1 bronze ) Year Age 18 km 50 km 4 × 10 km relay 1936 26 Bronze 8 — World Championships [ edit ] 3 medals – ( 1 gold , 1 silver , 1 bronze ) Year Age 18 km\nDocument 3: Keminmaa, Finland  \nDied 21 December 1993 (aged 84)  \nKittilä, Finland  \nHeight 170 cm (5 ft 7 in)  \nWeight 66 kg (146 lb)  \nSport: Ice Hockey  \nClub: Kittilän Urheilijat  \nMedal record  \nMen's ice hockey  \nRepresenting Finland  \nOlympic Games  \n1936 Garmisch-Partenkirchen Tournament  \nWorld Championships  \n1937 Chamonix Tournament  \n1937 Chamonix Team Event  \nJuho Pekka Niemi (born Yliniemi, 14 November 1909 – 21 December 1993) was a Finnish ice hockey player who competed at the 1936 Winter Olympics. He won a bronze medal in the team event.\nDocument 4: Pekka Niemi (ice hockey player) - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random article About Wikipedia Contact us Contribute Help Learn to edit Community portal Recent changes Upload file Special pages Search Search Appearance Donate Create account Log in Personal tools Donate Create account Log in Pages for logged out editors learn more Contributions Talk Contents move to sidebar hide ( Top ) 1 Ice Hockey results Toggle Ice Hockey results subsection 1.1 Olympic Games 1.2 World Championships 2 References 3 External links Toggle the table of contents\nDocument 5: Pekka Niemi (weightlifter) Pekka Kalevi Niemi (born 14 November 1952) is a retired Finnish heavyweight weightlifter who competed at the 1980 and 1984 Olympics; he finished tenth in 1980 and won a bronze medal in 1984. Niemi took part in every major international competition between 1977 and 1984, with the best results of fifth-seventh place at the European championships of 1983–84. He did not expect to medal at the 1984 Olympics, and after finishing his attempts went for sightseeing. The officials delayed the award ceremony by a few hours trying to find him, but failed, and went ahead with the\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the val